This application bundles a dataset (assets/data/theographic.json) derived from
Theographic Bible Metadata by Robert Rouse / Viz.Bible,
https://github.com/robertrouse/theographic-bible-metadata, licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Changes: converted to a
compact JSON form by scripts/build_theographic.dart (record links resolved to
array indexes, Easton's dictionary text flattened to plain text, verse ids
decoded to book/chapter/verse references); one corrected verse link ("Death of
Moses" pointed to Genesis 34:1 upstream, a book/verse-ID collision, corrected
to Deuteronomy 34:1). As a derivative of that dataset, assets/data/theographic.json
is itself licensed CC BY-SA 4.0; the application code remains under the Apache
License 2.0.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This application bundles a dataset (assets/data/places.json) derived from
Bible-Geocoding-Data by OpenBible.info,
https://github.com/openbibleinfo/Bible-Geocoding-Data, licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Changes: converted to a
compact JSON form by tool/build_places.dart (one representative modern
coordinate chosen per ancient place, verse ids decoded to book/chapter/verse
references). As a derivative of that dataset, assets/data/places.json is
itself licensed CC BY 4.0; the application code remains under the Apache
License 2.0.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
lib/data/importer/curated_journeys_data.dart contains hand-authored Atlas
journey waypoints (people and places the bundled datasets above don't
otherwise link with enough detail to plot a real route). It cross-references
those datasets by their own identifiers (bible_people.slug from Theographic
Bible Metadata, places.name from Bible-Geocoding-Data) for interoperability,
but its content — which verse establishes each waypoint, and which place it
resolves to — is independently researched against the source text, not
copied or adapted from either bundled dataset. It is licensed under the
Apache License 2.0 along with the rest of the application code.
